Subject: Move kiota-js packages to 1.0.0-preview.102 for apicurio-registry-ui 3.2
Origin: DHI-internal (DHI dependency alignment for the 3.2 UI build)
Description: Move the six @microsoft/kiota-* packages from 1.0.0-preview.99 to 1.0.0-preview.102 in the typescript-sdk peer ranges and the ui-app direct dependencies, and regenerate both lockfiles.
CVE: CVE-2026-49336
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/Apicurio/apicurio-registry 80b51a694b7176b06654d3b8cb9c6f295a3838d3
Regenerate: `npm install --package-lock-only --ignore-scripts`
Verify: sbom pkg:npm/%40microsoft/kiota-http-fetchlibrary@1.0.0-preview.102
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI 3.2 line dependency alignment; the 3.3 line already pins a newer kiota-js set)
Drop-When: never: the 3.2 upstream branch keeps the kiota-js preview.99 pins, so this patch stays until the 3.2 line is retired

The kiota-http-fetchlibrary 1.0.0-preview.99 release carries CVE-2026-49336, and preview.102 is the earliest kiota-js release that fixes it within the preview line. The typescript-sdk package pins the kiota-js set as exact peers, so moving only the direct dependency leaves a mixed set that npm resolves as a conflict, which is why all six packages move together. The pipeline applies this patch only on the 3.2 line because the include is shared with 3.3.

